A||||3||Scott_M||Code 23 on a 4 cyl..?||||1||
Z||000000||Scott_M||07-07-2000||11:52 PM||||If've been getting a code 23 for some time now. However, the manual says this is only applicable for the 6 cyl fieros, so what gives. I've replaced the O2 sensor and the MAT sensor. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||07-07-2000||11:53 PM||||What year 4 cyl? I think there are code changes on the 87/88 DIS 4cyl's.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||07-08-2000||12:23 PM||||go find your motor in the ECM quick ref and the 4 cyl lists in the cave link at the bottom of this page.<P>You have an 87+ 4 cyl. You have a MAT sensor. It is located right of the TBI sticking straight out the top of the intake. You can now disrequard nearly ALL the haynes/chiltons material for your motor. They are not correct for 87 88.<P>replace it. dont's even fool with it. Get e BorgWarner replacement unit. If you cannot get BorgWarner, you want the kind that has a plastic guard over the sensor elelment, NOT the metal guard. (The metal ones will work but respond more slowly to changes in manifold temp. This is not acceptable in the 4 cyl.) The actual sensor is the little disk under the guard.<P>DO NOT over tighten this sensor or you can split the manifold! Use ONLY teflon sealing tape on the threads. Tighten only enough for a good seal.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Scott_M||07-08-2000||04:18 PM||||Thanks guys. You know when I went to get the MAP sensor I mistakenly asked for the MAT sensor and had to take it back after I realized my "mistake". Almost put it too. Oh well...Thanks again, This site rocks!||||reg||1
